 //! Constants: a [`ConstTree`] as a JavaScript expression at a type, the hoisted-constant names v1
 //! shares, the caller `Location` value, and the `static` initializer (v1 `backend/src/constant.rs`
 //! and `intrinsics.rs::caller_location_value`, over the decoded tree instead of an allocation).
+//!
+//! # Pooled constants
+//!
+//! A [`ConstTree::Reference`] or [`ConstTree::Slice`] node is the pointee of a pointer into
+//! anonymous memory, and the producer only encodes memory rustc interned **immutable**
+//! (`backend/src/jir/encode.rs::check_const_memory` declines every other allocation, nested ones
+//! included). Under a shared reference that memory can only ever be read, so one JavaScript object
+//! may stand for it at every use: [`poolable`] is the structural half of that rule, and
+//! `link/pool.rs` the whole-program half (host exposure, reuse, economics). A node the program-wide
+//! selection names is spelled as its binding, `pool$h<hash of type and text>`; everything else is
+//! spelled exactly as before. The selection reaches this module through a [`PoolScope`] the lane
+//! driver installs around its final lowering pass — the lowering context has no field for it — so
+//! every other lowering (the physical ABI's cost trials, the representation probes) spells every
+//! constant inline, as it always did.
